# For device attestation, Veridact holds no signing secret — devices sign,
# Veridact only verifies (decisions/0002). decisions/0010 adds a separate,
# second kind of key: Veridact's OWN self-signed C2PA signing certificate,
# used to emit standard C2PA manifests (Veridact vouching for what it
# directly observed at capture — timestamp, device, challenge — not
# forging a device's own attestation). Auto-generated on first use; never
# committed, same reasoning as the runtime database below.
c2pa_signing/
*.db
__pycache__/
.venv/
